// Source only, for consumers that need `dist` and nothing else.
//
// `tsconfig.json` is the project: source, tests, and the tooling they need. This is the subset a
// *build* needs — the compiled output another package imports.
//
// It exists because the frontend deploy compiles this package so `apps/web/vite.config.ts` can
// import `@mintro/engine`, and Netlify's install carries no test runner. Building the full project
// there typechecks `test/**`, which imports `vitest`, which is a root devDependency that a
// production install has no reason to install. Seventy-two errors, every one in a test file, none
// in `src`.
//
// Nothing here narrows what `npm run check` covers. The root build still uses `tsconfig.json` and
// still typechecks every test.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"]
}
